Presidential elections were held in [[Lithuania]] on 11 May 2014, with a second round held on 25 May between the top two candidates from the first round.<ref>[http://www.electionguide.org/elections/id/2388/ Lithuania] IFES</ref> In the second round, incumbent [[President of Lithuania|President]] [[Dalia Grybauskaitė]] was re-elected with 58% of the vote. Second round took place alongside the [[2014 European Parliament election in Lithuania|2014 European elections]].

==Electoral changes==
Since these elections all potential voters, living permanently or temporarily outside of [[Republic of Lithuania]], had to submit documents to Central Election Commission's register.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.renkuosilietuva.lt/lt/rinkimai-lietuvoje-/|title=Lietuvoje organizuojami rinkimai - Renkuosi Lietuvą}}</ref>

==Participating candidates==
Initially 12 candidates were officially confirmed to participate,<ref>{{cite web|author=ELTA |url=http://www.delfi.lt/news/daily/lithuania/r-paksas-tai-buvo-spjuvis.d?id=64163158 |title=Candidates |publisher=Delfi.lt |date=1 March 2014 |accessdate=28 May 2014}}</ref> but only 7 fulfilled the criterion of 20,000 supporting signatures.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://vz.lt/article/2014/4/4/prezidentas-bus-renkamas-is-septyniu-kandidatu |title=Prezidentas bus renkamas iš septynių kandidatų |publisher=Vz.lt |date=4 April 2014 |accessdate=28 May 2014 |archive-date=6 May 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140506044403/http://vz.lt/article/2014/4/4/prezidentas-bus-renkamas-is-septyniu-kandidatu |url-status=dead }}</ref>
* [[Zigmantas Balčytis]] ([[Social Democratic Party of Lithuania|Social Democratic Party]]), [[Member of the European Parliament]]
* [[Dalia Grybauskaitė]], incumbent [[President of Lithuania]] (2009–2014)
* [[Artūras Paulauskas]] ([[Labour Party (Lithuania)|Labour Party]]), member of [[Seimas]]
* [[Naglis Puteikis]], member of [[Seimas]]
* [[Bronis Ropė]] ([[Lithuanian Peasant and Greens Union]]), Mayor of [[Ignalina]]
* [[Valdemar Tomaševski]], [[Member of the European Parliament]]
* [[Artūras Zuokas]] ([[YES (Lithuanian political party)|YES]]), Mayor of [[Vilnius]]

Grybauskaitė was supported by the [[Homeland Union]] and [[Liberal Movement (Lithuania)|Liberal Movement]].

Unsuccessful candidates include: [[Rolandas Paksas]], {{ill|Linas Balsys (politician)|lt|Linas Balsys (1961)|lt=Linas Balsys}}, {{ill|Kristina Brazauskienė|lt}}, {{ill|Vladas Lašas|lt|Vladas Lašas (1956)}}, [[Jonas Lašinis]] and [[Rolandas Paulauskas]].

